# Mosquitto ACL for the Phoenix MQTT protocol (topics phoenix/v1/...).
#
# Phoenix Core reads every node's uplink and writes every node's downlink and
# its own retained status.
user phoenix-core
topic readwrite phoenix/v1/#

# Every other user is a node agent whose user name is its deviceId (for a
# TLS-PSK listener with use_identity_as_username, its PSK identity). It may
# publish only on its own uplink, read only its own downlink, and read Core's
# status. A node therefore cannot impersonate, or eavesdrop on, another node.
pattern write phoenix/v1/nodes/%u/up/#
pattern read phoenix/v1/nodes/%u/down/#
pattern read phoenix/v1/core/status
